{
  "title": "Rainy Season, Stiff Body? 4 Yoga Poses That Can Help Ease Joint Pain And Muscle Stiffness",
  "publication_date": "2026-07-26T07:40:02Z",
  "summary": "Himalayan Siddhaa Akshar of Akshar Yoga Kendraa says the monsoon can increase muscle stiffness and joint aches as people become less active. She offers four simple yoga poses to improve flexibility, support joint health and maintain movement during the rainy season. Gentle, regular practice and medical advice for chronic conditions are recommended.",
  "content": "The rainy season may bring cooler temperatures and lush surroundings, but it can also lead to stiff muscles and achy joints as people spend more time indoors and stay less active. Himalayan Siddhaa Akshar, founder of Akshar Yoga Kendraa, author and spiritual leader, shares four simple yoga poses that can improve flexibility, support joint health and help you stay active during the monsoon.\n\nRegular gentle movement helps maintain circulation and prevents stiffness. The four poses recommended focus on improving range of motion around key joints, lengthening tight muscles and encouraging mindful breathing. Practicing them daily for a few minutes can reduce discomfort and make everyday activities easier. Beginners should move slowly, respect pain limits and modify poses to suit their ability.\n\nThose with existing joint conditions or chronic pain should consult a healthcare professional before beginning a new exercise routine. In many cases, a tailored approach with modifications and guidance from a qualified instructor can make yoga a safe, low-impact option for maintaining mobility.\n\nBeyond individual poses, maintaining light activity, good hydration and attention to posture during the monsoon months can help preserve joint health. Short, consistent yoga sessions integrated into daily life offer a practical way to counteract stiffness and support overall well-being during periods of reduced outdoor activity.",
